    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 2719765,
        "name": "Skadoos",
        "username": "Skadoos",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/skadoos/{size}/409261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-05-20T07:45:08.644Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It’s probably time to introduce some guidelines with respect to the usage of content generated by LLMs/GenAIs. I feel like there should be a policy, in either direction.</p>\n<p>Personally I find it annoying. If I wanted to debate an LLM with its incorrect takes and infinite patience, or to look at anatomically incorrect hands, I’d go do that somewhere else.</p>\n<p>Although I’m aware that ultimately the moderation team would have to identify the content as such and any rules against it would probably be difficult to enforce unless it’s obvious, it’d be nice to at least get a guideline out there, and depending on the specifics, an additional reason to flag posts.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "posts_count": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-05-20T07:45:08.644Z",
